F-0054 hook patch, written by Smith 3 Nov 2026 20:15. Not applied: a scheduled run cannot edit the hook.

Why: the hook lets node run only a script under the folder or `node -e`, so `node --version` (P-0300,
2 Nov) and `node --experimental-strip-types <script>` (25 Oct) each cost a denied call. Neither does
anything a `.cjs` under the folder cannot: --version only prints, and the TypeScript flag is stripped
like python3 -I so the script that follows must still be under the folder. The child branch strips
the flag too, or a child could run a parent script by putting the flag first (the script check reads
parts[1]). bun stays denied: a second JS runtime is a new install, not a flag.

Proof without the hook: python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0054-check.py

Apply from an interactive session:
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply --check /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0054.diff
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0054.diff
  python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/test-hook.py        (6 new cases)
and close: python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/findings.py fix F-0054 --commit <hash> --note 'node --version and --experimental-strip-types on folder scripts allowed; bun stays denied'
Line numbers are against 6f41d52 (3 Nov).

